                "senderName": "NWS Spokane WA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 12 at 7:41PM PDT until September 13 at 8:00PM PDT by NWS Spokane WA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Debris and ash flows, rock slides, and minor flooding caused\nby excessive rainfall is possible, especially near burn scars.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of North Central and Northeast Washington,\nincluding the following counties, in North Central Washington,\nChelan, Douglas and Okanogan. In Northeast Washington, Ferry.\n\n* WHEN...From 1 AM PDT Sunday through Sunday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in debris and ash flows over\nburn scars in steep terrain.  Rock slides will be possible.  Minor\nflooding in urban areas where there is poor drainage. Storm drains\nand ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A slow moving storm system will bring persistent bands of rain\nthrough Central Washington.  Moderate to heavy rain intensities\nare expected at times.  Rainfall amounts will range between 0.50\nand 1.50 inches with locally around 2.00 inches in southern\nChelan County.\n- This includes but is not limited to the following burn scars:\nModrite, Kaiser Canyon, Sinlahekin, Chelan Falls, Little Giant,\nSisi, and Pioneer.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
